      "taskType": "reverseReasoning",
      "prompt": "Let $f(x)=(x-({{h}}))^2{{k|signed}}$ and $g(x)={{h}}-\\sqrt{x-({{k}})}$. Use both compositions and the necessary domain restrictions to decide whether $g=f^{-1}$.",
      "responseFields": [
        {
          "id": "fog",
          "label": "On the domain of $g$, simplify $f(g(x))$",
          "inputProfile": "expression",
          "expected": "x"
        },
        {
          "id": "gof",
          "label": "After restricting $f$ correctly, simplify $g(f(x))$",
          "inputProfile": "expression",
          "expected": "x"
        },
        {
          "id": "f-domain",
          "label": "Required domain restriction on $f$",
          "inputProfile": "choice",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "left",
              "label": "$x\\le {{h}}$"
            },
            {
              "id": "right",
              "label": "$x\\ge {{h}}$"
            },
            {
              "id": "all",
              "label": "All real x"
            }
          ],
          "expected": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "g-domain",
          "label": "Domain required for $f(g(x))$",
          "inputProfile": "choice",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "from-k",
              "label": "$x\\ge {{k}}$"
            },
            {
              "id": "from-h",
              "label": "$x\\le {{h}}$"
            },
            {
              "id": "all",
              "label": "All real x"
            }
          ],
          "expected": "from-k"
        },
        {
          "id": "conclusion",
          "label": "Conclusion",
          "inputProfile": "choice",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "yes-left",
              "label": "Yes, when $f$ is restricted to its left branch."
            },
            {
              "id": "yes-right",
              "label": "Yes, only on the right branch."
            },
            {
              "id": "no",
              "label": "No, the negative square-root branch can never be an inverse."
            }
          ],
          "expected": "yes-left"
        }
      ],
      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "The negative square-root expression reverses the left branch.",
        "reasoning": [
          "$f(g(x))=x$ for inputs in the square-root domain $x\\ge {{k}}$.",
          "$g(f(x))={{h}}-\\sqrt{(x-({{h}}))^2}={{h}}-|x-{{h}}|$.",
          "When $x\\le {{h}}$, $|x-{{h}}|={{h}}-x$, so the reverse composition becomes x."
        ],
        "answerSummary": "They are inverses when $f$ is restricted to $x\\le {{h}}$."
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "The sign in front of the square root tells you which side of the quadratic is being reversed."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
        "On the left of the vertex, $|x-h|=h-x$."
      ],
      "generator": {
        "parameters": {
          "h": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": -5,
            "max": 5
          },
          "k": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": -5,
            "max": 5
          }
        }
      }
